      "math_academy_id": "e-12904",
      "problem": "A horizontal line in the $xy$-plane passes through the point $(- 2,4).$ What is the equation of the line? Does the point $(4,-2)$ lie on that line?",
      "worked_solution": "Since the horizontal line passes through $(-2,4)$, every point on the line has a $y$-coordinate of $4.$ So, the equation of that line is $y=4.$\n\nThe $y$-coordinate of the point $(4,-2)$ is $-2,$ but all points on the line $y=4$ have a $y$-coordinate of $4.$ So, the point $(4,-2)$ is not on the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14166027/assets/0fa994fe8d3da1428d803aa0c6d6c1470eab0fd23e24cd0edd67bb213efec068.png)",
